  "source": {
    "prompt": "Create one controllable sticker of the friendly orange cat in the attached artwork. Preserve its exact style, identity, colors and accessories. Use expressive cartoon proportions, bold clean outlines, saturated colors, simple shading, and a crisp die-cut sticker edge. This is a catalog demonstration, no lettering and no unrelated scenery. Use exactly one sprite character with a stable front-facing face region. Use pose control id pose with exactly these 8 clip IDs, in this order: idle, wave, bounce, sway, wiggle, hop, spin, dance. Idle must visibly breathe and blink; every pose is a distinct animated looping body action, never a still or a whole-image transform. Keep the face region visible and stable; spin means a playful partial body twist with the face kept forward. Use 6 frames per clip and a 2-second loop. Use mood control id mood with exactly three expression IDs: neutral, happy, surprised. Independent pose and mood controls must combine correctly. Preserve the selected style in all frames. Return a production sprite plan using the normal sprite source; render the approval reference before building.",
    "catalogVersion": "2026-09-16.1",
